From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: v0lumehi <aljic.zijad@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 13:59:49 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] build_ipa_from_nsp: a derived profile without frame step
 stubs keeps the game's own step

Tears of the Kingdom 1.4.2 ran at double speed. The profile registers only 1.4.3, so a derived profile packs 1.4.2. The profile's patches.py has FRAME_STEP stubs for the 1.4.3 main only. The 1.4.2 main gets no frame step state page, and derive_profile copied fps_target 60 unchanged. Without the page, fps_present_cap() returns 60, present_itv() presents every vsync, and the game steps 1/30 s per frame.

derive_profile now reads the FRAME_STEP table of the profile's patches.py with ast (the file is never run). When the table has entries and none is for the derived main's build ID, the derived profile gets fps_target 0, with a comment line that says why. Registered builds, shader_only derivations and profiles without FRAME_STEP are unchanged.

Reported in LNPANDY/NX2Apple#303, traced by fredchu.

Upstream-Status: forwarded seedds/nxnative#794
Reason: A derived profile with frame step stubs for other builds only kept fps_target 60, so Tears of the Kingdom 1.4.2 ran at double speed
Issue: LNPANDY/NX2Apple#303

Co-authored-by: Fred Chu <1243384+fredchu@users.noreply.github.com>

